cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WaRF in your research, please cite the software as below."
type: software
title: "WaRF: Weighted n-Agent Reliability Framework"
abstract: >-
  WaRF reviews code with a panel of LLM personas. Each vote is weighted by the
  agent's learned, domain-specific reliability (a Beta posterior updated from
  ground-truth labels), and the weighted evidence accumulates under a
  sequential probability ratio test, so a review stops as soon as a statistical
  boundary is crossed and reports a confidence level alongside its verdict.
authors:
  - family-names: Heydarov
    given-names: Teymur
version: 0.1.0
# Set to the date of the first public release; currently the date of the talk.
date-released: 2026-09-25
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/teymurheydarov/WaRF"
keywords:
  - code review
  - multi-agent systems
  - large language models
  - sequential probability ratio test
  - calibration
references:
